(6516211, 967950, 123348, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mbrutus2009:</b></div><hr/><i> This looks awesome! I have always wanted to go to California. Because it is advanced editing I would have gotten rid of that thing in the water... Boat? Rock? Either way it is a touch distracting to the horizon line. Other than that this is awesome! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thank you for your comment! :) The things in the water are rocks, huge rocks and also it might look better without them that is what it looks like in reality and  since I have have driven by there hundreds of times over the years I would probably notice that they were missing :)<br/>and according to DPC rules would have been disqualified for removing them. (<u>You may NOT</u> use ANY editing tool to move, <u>remove</u> or duplicate <u>any element of your photograph</u> <u>that would change a typical viewers description of the photograph</u> (aside from color or crop), even if the tool is otherwise legal, and regardless of whether you intended the change when the photograph was taken.)<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by mbrutus2009: This looks awesome! I have always wanted to go to California. Because it is advanced editing I would have gotten rid of that thing in the water... Boat? Rock? Either way it is a touch distracting to the horizon line. Other than that this is awesome!  Thank you for your comment! :) The things in the water are rocks, huge rocks and also it might look better without them that is what it looks like in reality and  since I have have driven by there hundreds of times over the years I would probably notice that they were missing :)and according to DPC rules would have been disqualified for removing them. (You may NOT use ANY editing tool to move, remove or duplicate any element of your photograph that would change a typical viewers description of the photograph (aside from color or crop), even if the tool is otherwise legal, and regardless of whether you intended the change when the photograph was taken.)', '2011-08-26 01:43:24.000000', NULL, 0),
